  {
    "n": 82,
    "source": "For C++11 compiler, it is also possible to use the {1} by defining {2} and {3}. If your schemas do not need {4} and {5}, you can set both macros to zero to disable this feature, which will reduce some code size.",
    "tokens": [
      "<span class=\"tt\">std::regex</span>",
      "<span class=\"tt\">RAPIDJSON_SCHEMA_USE_INTERNALREGEX=0</span>",
      "<span class=\"tt\">RAPIDJSON_SCHEMA_USE_STDREGEX=1</span>",
      "<span class=\"tt\">pattern</span>",
      "<span class=\"tt\">patternProperties</span>"
    ],
    "ja": "C++11コンパイラーでは、{2}と{3}を定義することで、{1}も使えます。スキーマで{4}と{5}が不要なら、両方のマクロを0にしてこの機能を無効にすると、コードサイズをいくらか小さくできます。"
  },
